// docs/spec/en/07-constexpr-and-consteval.md (ch09) §9.1(4): every
// potentially-evaluated call to an immediate function shall produce a
// constant expression. An array bound is a constant-expression
// (docs/spec/en/05-unions-and-packed-layout.md (ch05) §9.4(2)), so an
// immediate call is a legal bound and, like the namespace-scope initializer
// case, this position cannot be satisfied by a runtime evaluation at all.
// docs/spec/en/06-constant-evaluation.md (ch06) §7.2(6.2) requires the
// implementation to support the call; §7.2(6.4) covers the `sizeof` query
// used to observe the resulting bound.
//
// Call position: array bound. Callee: free `consteval` function.
//
// Expected value derived from the spec text above and independently confirmed
// with `clang++-22 -std=c++26`, which compiles this exact source and exits 42.
consteval int twice(int x) {
    return x * 2;
}

int main() {
    char buffer[twice(21)];
    if (sizeof(buffer) != 42) {
        return 1;
    }
    return 42;
}
